xt extraction version; withdrawn by the seal (D379). Details: `docs/research/2026-11-06-e1-no-home-drops/README.md`, PRD 11 E1.\n146:5. **Historical coverage-start reading, retired by D370** (D364–D366): the capital-spending line is missed in about one read in six (the question is then left as it was); a labelled guidance figure is written with the fact tier; later reports reach the questions only through the daily stream; `scripts/preflight.py` does not replay the reading's check.\n343:  probe (18 stored requests, unchanged and changed ×3, about $0.15) was sent 2026-11-16 to `poc/data/clean-unlisted-probe-2026-11-16/`\n346:- **The unlisted-parts probe (D578 to D580):** negative under the rule fixed before the send. The changed written answers left no part\n402:  - **Slice 4b (D598, corrected in D599 and D600):** one writer per store by an operating-system lock, preflight's one locked copy, the\n413:- preflight's locked copy and the snapshot route;\n471:Before the pilot: the census and the version-2 probe passed their gates (D702, D705); poc-v120 was built (D706); the paid design and\n485:  version with the decided dependencies, tested at $0 on the request text, then a few cents. Alex chose A (D691). The probe passed\n486:  its registered rule (D692, [RESULT.md](research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md), $0.0176): linked to\n499:  whole-window measurement, designed with the council at $0 first. The link census passed its gate (D702); Alex chose to probe a\n528:- **The probe and its rule** are written before any J2 send. Its regression guard is the frozen judgement gold: the stored v7 requests\n570:  - **The one-outcome probe failed its line 1** (`docs/research/2026-11-19-one-outcome-probe/RESULT.md`): it fixes the period bundles\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,re\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport probe,probe_read,probe_rehearsal as r\np=r.PLAN\nexpected=set(); cutoff=[]; overlaps=[]\nstart=re.compile(r'\\\\''\"'^- (e'\"\\\\d+) \\\\[|\"'^- (v'\"\\\\d+) \\\\('\\\\'',re.M)\nsection=re.compile(r'\\\\''\"'^'\"\\\\[(?:Current conclusions|Themes in force|Previous conclusion)|\"'^Answer per'\"'\\\\'',re.M)\nfor part in ('\\\\''refused'\\\\'','\\\\''matched'\\\\''):\n    for i in p[part]:\n        key=probe.key_of(i); user=i['\\\\''user'\\\\'']; lines=probe_read.entries(user)\n        starts=list(start.finditer(user)); cuts=sorted([x.start() for x in starts]+[x.start() for x in section.finditer(user)]+[len(user)])\n        overlap=set(i['\\\\''lists'\\\\'']['\\\\''dependencies'\\\\'']) & set(i['\\\\''lists'\\\\'']['\\\\''themes'\\\\''])\n        if overlap: overlaps.append((key,overlap))\n        for m in starts:\n            k=m.group(1) or m.group(2); end=next(x for x in cuts if x>m.start()); full=user[m.start():end].strip('\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'')\n            rendered=lines.get(k)\n            if not full.startswith(rendered or '\\\\'''\\\\'') or rendered\"'!=full:\n                extra=full[len(rendered or '\"'\\\\'''\\\\''):].strip('\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'')\n                if extra and not extra.startswith('\\\\''- the '\\\\''):\n                    cutoff.append((part,key,k,len(rendered or '\\\\'''\\\\''),repr(extra[:200])))\nprint('\\\\''overlapping dependency and theme IDs'\\\\'',overlaps)\nprint('\\\\''truncated distinct'\\\\'',len(cutoff), '\\\\''examples'\\\\'', cutoff[:15])\nprint('\\\\''stored answers affected'\\\\'',[(part,key,k) for part,key,k,*rest in cutoff if k in (lambda a:a.get('\\\\''cites'\\\\'',[])+[x['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\''] for x in a.get('\\\\''pushes'\\\\'',[])]+a.get('\\\\''cites_views'\\\\'',[])+[x['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''] for x in a.get('\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'',[])])(json.loads(r.BY_KEY[key]['\\\\''stored answer'\\\\'']))][:20])\nall_a=r.clean_answers()\nfor cls,support in [('\\\\''ambiguous'\\\\'',True),('\\\\''ambiguous'\\\\'',False)]:\n    b=r.clean_readings({f'\\\\''B/control-1:8807|{d}|e393'\\\\'':{'\\\\''class'\\\\'':cls,'\\\\''valid_support'\\\\'':support} for d in (1,2,3)})\n    print('\\\\''nonambiguous 8807 labeled'\\\\'',cls,support,'\\\\''->'\\\\'',r.verdict_of(all_a,b))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
