{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The packets still omit source text the model saw, and the verdict still accepts an ambiguity label that can hide a material loss.\n\n1. **Preserve multiline quotes.** I found 14 planned entries where the parser drops text after an unindented continuation line. One is `old-2:6955`’s `e4070`, which the saved answer cites. The missing line gives the expected first-half-2027 closing date. The rehearsal compares the packet against the same parser, so it misses this loss. Check the packet against the original request text for a multiline quote. [Packet parser](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:35) · [Rehearsal assertion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_rehearsal.py:216)\n2. **Enforce the frozen ambiguity labels.** All three `8807` readings can be marked `ambiguous` with `valid_support: true`, and the verdict returns **pass**. The frozen target is the $393B reference and has two valid sources. Allow the neutral `ambiguous` class only for targets premarked ambiguous, and exclude those readings from support counts. [Reading validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:52) · [Frozen target](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json:210)"}}
